Spectral and Source Serif 4 (self-hosted web fonts)
====================================================

Used by the @font-face rules in docs/blog/*.html (the four blog articles
and the blog index) and in docs/de/index.html for --font-display
(Spectral) and --font-body (Source Serif 4). Self-hosted so the pages
carry no external font CDN (Google Fonts or otherwise) — see CLAUDE.md's
font policy.

These two families were fetched once before (commit fc47183) but removed
again by a later, unrelated redesign (commit 241e926) that moved
docs.html and docs/index.html (EN) to Sora + JetBrains Mono and never
touched docs/de/index.html or the older blog scaffold, both of which kept
declaring Spectral/Source Serif 4 by path — docs/de/index.html was never
migrated to the newer design at all (it is also still on version 1.0.0 in
several places; a separate, larger gap than fonts). Every @font-face rule
on both pointed at files that no longer existed for months; the browser
fell back to the declared Georgia fallback, so nothing visibly broke, but
nothing was actually self-hosted either. Refetched here and pinned with
this file so it can't happen again silently; tests/test_v160_design.py's
`test_every_docs_font_face_url_resolves_to_a_real_file` now asserts every
@font-face url() under docs/ resolves to a real file.

Source
------

Both fetched from their official @fontsource npm packages (the same
distribution method the DejaVu font in app/fonts/ documents, and the one
Sora/JetBrains Mono in this same directory already use):

  @fontsource/spectral@5.3.0
    https://registry.npmjs.org/@fontsource/spectral/-/spectral-5.3.0.tgz
    sha512-2TL5WWGOZj4SIsBmPFEzKeA60tXXd1Qp1OqaaVEWkJL8IfSGLk6YmiusmC441iFkdJDIuFelu1r8lhCmQUU3mw==

  @fontsource/source-serif-4@5.3.0
    https://registry.npmjs.org/@fontsource/source-serif-4/-/source-serif-4-5.3.0.tgz
    sha512-yQz8xmIgMzks8zQbpuca3UYtjxK798XCyQAGdDXmzBgvV7sdoK6d0YvE9F9kiYxORCEMRBgGZDZsSYcXj5KvwA==

Both integrity values were checked against the `dist.integrity` field the
npm registry publishes for that exact version (`npm view <pkg>@<version>
dist.integrity`) before any file was copied out of the tarball.

Files taken, unmodified, from each package's files/ directory — only the
weights/styles some page actually declares, nothing extra:

  spectral-latin-400-normal.woff2       blog + de/index.html
  spectral-latin-400-italic.woff2       de/index.html only
  spectral-latin-500-normal.woff2       de/index.html only
  spectral-latin-600-normal.woff2       de/index.html only
  spectral-latin-600-italic.woff2       de/index.html only
  spectral-latin-700-normal.woff2       blog + de/index.html
  spectral-latin-ext-400-normal.woff2   blog only
  spectral-latin-ext-700-normal.woff2   blog only
  source-serif-4-latin-300-normal.woff2      blog + de/index.html
  source-serif-4-latin-400-normal.woff2      blog + de/index.html
  source-serif-4-latin-400-italic.woff2      de/index.html only
  source-serif-4-latin-600-normal.woff2      blog + de/index.html
  source-serif-4-latin-700-normal.woff2      de/index.html only
  source-serif-4-latin-ext-300-normal.woff2  blog only
  source-serif-4-latin-ext-400-normal.woff2  blog only
  source-serif-4-latin-ext-600-normal.woff2  blog only

Only the blog pages split `latin`/`latin-ext` into separate @font-face
rules with a `unicode-range` each (the exact ranges fontsource publishes
for those subsets) — `latin` alone (U+0000-00FF plus general punctuation)
already covers every character the current German/English blog text uses,
including German umlauts and the „…" quotes, but `latin-ext` (Latin
Extended-A/B, e.g. Polish/Czech/Hungarian diacritics) is shipped and wired
in too, so a future article naming a person or place with those characters
renders in the real typeface instead of silently falling back to Georgia.
docs/de/index.html predates that split; it declares one `latin`-only rule
per weight/style, unchanged here — only the missing files it already
referenced were added, not a redesign of its CSS.

License
-------

SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 — full text as shipped by each
package, unmodified: spectral-LICENSE (Spectral, copyright 2017 The
Spectral Project Authors) and source-serif-4-LICENSE (Source Serif 4).
Permissive, attribution-preserving, explicitly allows embedding and
redistribution; compatible with this project's GPLv3.

Also in this directory
-----------------------

sora-latin-*.woff2 and JetBrainsMono-*.woff2 are unrelated: they serve
docs/docs.html and docs/index.html (EN — the newer "Signal design
system"), fetched the same way (@fontsource), not covered by this fix —
left untouched.
